      <li><a href={wiki('Military rank')}>Military rank</a>, Wikipedia: the grades, and where the names came from.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('Chevron (insignia)')}>Chevron (insignia)</a>, Wikipedia: the history of chevrons, and which way they point.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('British Army officer rank insignia')}>British Army officer rank insignia</a>, Wikipedia: pips and crowns, and the move to the shoulder in 1880.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('Royal Navy officer rank insignia')}>Royal Navy officer rank insignia</a>, Wikipedia: sleeve rings and the curl of 1856.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('RAF officer ranks')}>RAF officer ranks</a>, Wikipedia: how an air force built its ranks on naval ones in 1919.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('United States Army enlisted rank insignia')}>United States Army enlisted rank insignia</a>, Wikipedia: chevrons, rockers and the change of direction in 1902.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('Warrant officer')}>Warrant officer</a> and <a href={wiki('Non-commissioned officer')}>Non-commissioned officer</a>, Wikipedia.</li>
      <li><a href={wiki('Waffenfarbe')}>Waffenfarbe</a>, Wikipedia: arm-of-service colours as piping.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="eu-muted">Last updated <time datetime={updated}>15 November 2026</time>.</p>
  </article>
</Page>

